{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-37551-r4630285","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Pudina Hilsa (Bengali Fish with Mint)","sourcePageId":37551,"sourceRevision":"4630285","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-04-12T20:29:06Z","sourceRevisionUser":"AdoniTzedek","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Pudina%20Hilsa%20(Bengali%20Fish%20with%20Mint)&oldid=4630285","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:46:08.534Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Baked recipes","Category:Bengali recipes","Category:Halal recipes","Category:Kosher for Passover recipes","Category:Main course recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using chile paste and sauce","Category:Recipes using fish","Category:Recipes using ginger paste","Category:Recipes using mint","Category:Recipes using sugar","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Very Easy recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"43f2012a746bad483def77a0cd1a517746984b31dfb798a7019821f45db15e0b","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Fish recipes\n| Difficulty = 1\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\n'''Pudina hilsa''' is a wonderful [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Bengal|Bengali]] preparation of hilsa fish. It is very easy and can be served hot with boiled rice.\n\n==Ingredients==\n*1 [[Cookbook:Kilogram|kg]] hilsa fish (kelee shad), cut into 10 pieces\n*1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Mint|pudina leaves (mint)]]\n*1 tsp [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]] paste\n*1 tsp [[Cookbook:Nutmeg|nutmeg]]\n* 50 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]] [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]], [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n*3 tbsp [[Cookbook:Capsicum|capsicum]]\n*[[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]] according to taste\n*1 [[Cookbook:Pinch|pinch]] of [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n*1 tsp green [[Cookbook:Chile Paste and Sauce|chili paste]]\n\n==Procedure==\n# Wash the fish thoroughly in water. \n# Put the salt, sugar, 25 g of butter and all the other ingredients into a [[Cookbook:Baking Dish|baking dish]].\n# Add the fish pieces and sprinkle the rest of the butter on the top.\n# [[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] at 200°[[Cookbook:Celsius|C]] until the fish turns golden in color or otherwise appears to be done.\n\n[[Category:Bengali recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fish]]\n[[Category:Baked recipes]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mint]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile paste and sauce]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ginger paste]]\n[[Category:Kosher for Passover recipes]]\n[[Category:Halal recipes]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Pudina Hilsa (Bengali Fish with Mint)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 kg hilsa fish (kelee shad), cut into 10 pieces","sourceText":"1 kg hilsa fish (kelee shad), cut into 10 pieces","amountText":"1 kg hilsa fish (kelee shad), cut into 10 pieces","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 tsp pudina leaves (mint)","sourceText":"1 tsp pudina leaves (mint)","amountText":"1 tsp pudina leaves (mint)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 tsp ginger paste","sourceText":"1 tsp ginger paste","amountText":"1 tsp ginger paste","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 tsp nutmeg","sourceText":"1 tsp nutmeg","amountText":"1 tsp nutmeg","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"50 g butter, chopped","sourceText":"50 g butter, chopped","amountText":"50 g butter, chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"3 tbsp capsicum","sourceText":"3 tbsp capsicum","amountText":"3 tbsp capsicum","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"Salt according to taste","sourceText":"Salt according to taste","amountText":"Salt according to taste","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"1 pinch of sugar","sourceText":"1 pinch of sugar","amountText":"1 pinch of sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"1 tsp green chili paste","sourceText":"1 tsp green chili paste","amountText":"1 tsp green chili paste","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null}],"steps":[{"n":1,"text":"Wash the fish thoroughly in water.","sourceText":"Wash the fish thoroughly in water.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":2,"text":"Put the salt, sugar, 25 g of butter and all the other ingredients into a baking dish.","sourceText":"Put the salt, sugar, 25 g of butter and all the other ingredients into a baking dish.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":3,"text":"Add the fish pieces and sprinkle the rest of the butter on the top.","sourceText":"Add the fish pieces and sprinkle the rest of the butter on the top.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":4,"text":"Bake at 200°C until the fish turns golden in color or otherwise appears to be done.","sourceText":"Bake at 200°C until the fish turns golden in color or otherwise appears to be done.","durationMinutes":null}],"nutrition":null,"gaps":["Research extraction only; no culinary/editorial review.","Ingredient quantities, un